{"text": "The latest 10-K says GOOGL can run into operating difficulties from acquisitions and other strategic arrangements, including failed approvals or integration problems, and that those could harm business, financial condition, and operating results [f_5e6b1b091b49]. It also says supply-chain disruptions, shortages, price increases, and limited-source components could delay infrastructure upgrades or product availability [f_2774ff0f0b59], and that security and privacy breaches could lead to legal, financial, and reputational harm [f_223bd5d8afc9].

The latest 10-Q adds that its operations and financial results remain subject to risks and uncertainties that could hurt business, reputation, financial condition, and operating results [f_112722493658]. It says investments in new businesses, products, services, and technologies may not be commercially viable or earn adequate returns [f_112722493658], that capital-markets access or debt-management problems could impair strategy and financial flexibility [f_f2c947f73f4c], and that AI-related products and other new offerings can raise ethical, technological, legal, regulatory, and other challenges that could hurt brands and demand [f_e881e8952c74].

Operating margin over the last four reported quarters was 30.5% [f_fba88e7cd1c0], 31.6% [f_fba88e7cd1c0], 36.1% [f_fba88e7cd1c0], and 34.0% [f_fba88e7cd1c0]. It rose through the third quarter, then slipped in the latest quarter versus the prior quarter, but it is still above the first quarter in the series [f_fba88e7cd1c0]."}
